<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Waffen-SS</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1940–1945</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Waffen-SS was the armed wing of the Nazi SS, which grew from a few regiments into an army of some 38 divisions during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>. It took in volunteers and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conscription">conscripts</a> from occupied and allied countries, including Latvian and Estonian legions. Its units committed many war crimes, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuremberg">Nuremberg</a> tribunal declared the SS a criminal organisation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/waffen-ss.jpg" alt="Waffen-SS" width="320" height="256" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wiegand · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bundesarchiv_Bild_101III-Wiegand-117-02,_Russland,_Kradsch%C3%BCtze,_Beiwagenkrad.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
